@AGENTS.md

## Claude Code skills

Project-specific Claude skills live in `.claude/skills/`; Claude Code loads them when the work matches. Keep skill boundaries orthogonal: `android-conventions` is the baseline ruleset and `android-feature-delivery` coordinates cross-layer work. Use `/android-feature-delivery <feature-description>` for the full research, planning, validation and documentation workflow of a larger feature.

- `android-conventions` - the slice, MVVM, the client, the session, strings and replacing the dev identity
- `android-build-verify` - choose the smallest sufficient Gradle compile, test or assemble task
- `android-feature-delivery` - coordinate multi-layer feature work and pull in companion skills
- `android-contract-alignment` - keep DTOs and `ApiService` equal to the OpenAPI contract
- `android-testing` - ViewModel, client and Compose UI test patterns
- `compose-design-system` - shared Compose UI language and reusable components
- `deploy-device` - build, install and launch the debug app on a connected device or emulator

## Android Claude Commands

- `/generate-clients` - validate the shared contract; this app's client is hand-written and checked by `ApiContractTest`
